        "assistantOnly": false,
        "productUserFactEligible": true,
        "status": "complete",
        "attempted": true,
        "judged": true,
        "correct": true,
        "answer": "Battery drain is such an annoying one, let's poke at it. First thing I'd do is open Settings then Battery and look at what's ranked at the top over the last 24 hours. Whatever's hogging it, that's your target.\nThen the usual levers. Screen brightness down or on auto, background app refresh off for anything you rarely open, location set to while using for most apps, and low power mode whenever you're out for a long stretch. Killing push notifications for noisy apps helps more than people expect too.\nIf none of that moves it, the battery itself might just be worn down. But you've got the power bank and the wireless pad already, so you're not exactly stranded either.",
